// pair_programming_loop_v2 — agent pair_part_brief.md.tftpl renders ONE
// part's brief from the planner's plan (data.internal.plan_json, jq-extracted;
// template vars stay strings — the workflow renders ONE slot's brief per
// agent call).

The pair loop v2 split the workstream into parts. Your part (as planned by
the planner, executed verbatim — you implement it, not re-plan it):

Part id: {{ .part_id }}
Effort lane: {{ .effort }}
Files you own (the part's full scope; nothing outside it):
{{ .files_claimed }}

Part brief:
{{ .brief }}

Part acceptance (what "done" means for this part):
{{ .acceptance }}

Workstream text (context; your edits stay inside the part's file list):

{{ .workstream }}

Work only inside the files listed above. Commit per unit of work; NEVER
push, fetch, clone, or ls-remote (the workflow owns upstream placement).
End the turn by calling the `submit_outcome` tool: `part_ready` with what
you built and verified in the reason field when the part meets its
acceptance, or `part_help` with the findings in the reason field when you
cannot complete the part as planned.
